{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Terach took Avram his son, to go to the land of Canaan.</b> For he was of the seed of Shem, and to them the land was given as a heritage, as it is written: 'and Canaan was a servant to them.' And Lot and Sarai went with them, who were brother and sister together with Terach and Avram, who were the heads and principal ones." "<b>And they went out with them from Ur of the Chaldeans.</b> At the command of HaShem, as it is written: 'I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldeans' — and according to this interpretation, it is indeed specified where He commanded him." "<b>And they came as far as Haran.</b> And Terach did not manage to come to the land of Canaan, and died in Haran. <b>Shleima, the order of the perasha of Noah.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "The phrase 'שלימא סדרא דפרשת נח' appears to be a colophon marking the completion of the section; 'Shleima' = 'completed,' followed by the identification of the portion. Rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:56.168355524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}